Priorities are source-review release recommendations, not CVSS or proof of a production incident. No credential-logging, cryptography, SQL-injection, sync-over-async or throw ex; defect was found in the authored code (see 2.1). The most important point: the message hand-off protocol (`INI` -> `SNDNG` -> `PROC`/`ERROR`) has no recovery path. Several ordinary failures (a missing procedure, an MQ outage mid-batch, a stop or crash between two statements, a failed final update) leave rows in a state that is never selected again and that nothing reports (SOM-I1, I3, I4, I5).
