3. What's Already Good
• Layering and DI. Application/Infrastructure/host split with interfaces IOperacionServicio and IRepositorioTomi<T>, constructor injection (OperacionServicio.cs:33-44 (../../SWIFT/Outgoing/SWF_OUT_MQ/AplicacionSwfOUTMQ/OperacionServicio.cs#L33)),
SimpleInjector with Verify() (ServicHost.cs:87 (../../SWIFT/Outgoing/SWF_OUT_MQ/SwfOUTMQ/ServicHost.cs#L87)) and a per-scope configuration clone (line 81), matching the baseline's DI/Repository intent.
• No secrets or payloads in first-party logs. The MQ password lives only in ConfiguracionMQ and the connection Hashtable (RepositorioTomi.cs:129,171 (../../SWIFT/Outgoing/SWF_OUT_MQ/InfraestructuraSwfOUTMQ/Repositorio/RepositorioTomi.cs#L129));
the four sensitive parameter keys are declared in a separate "sensitive" list (ConstantesServicio.cs:10 (../../SWIFT/Outgoing/SWF_OUT_MQ/AplicacionSwfOUTMQ/Enums/ConstantesServicio.cs#L10)) so the shared reader masks them; only MessageLength/StringLength of the SWIFT text is logged (line 226).
• TLS is mandatory by construction. Cipher spec, key repository and certificate label are *required* parameters, so the service cannot silently fall back to an unencrypted channel.
• Resource cleanup. Queue Close() and Disconnect() each have their own guarded try/catch in a finally (RepositorioTomi.cs:96-114 (../../SWIFT/Outgoing/SWF_OUT_MQ/InfraestructuraSwfOUTMQ/Repositorio/RepositorioTomi.cs#L96)), so a failing close cannot hide the original error or skip the disconnect.
• Exception hygiene. throw; (never throw ex;) in both update methods (lines 379, 411); the failure text carries folio and status.
• Parameterized SQL only, no string-built statements; stored procedures are the only DB surface.
• State finalization is in a `finally` (OperacionServicio.cs:102-105 (../../SWIFT/Outgoing/SWF_OUT_MQ/AplicacionSwfOUTMQ/OperacionServicio.cs#L102)), so GEN-7 (state left "running" after a failure) is not present here.
• Input checks before sending: null operation/queue, empty folio and empty message are detected per row (RepositorioTomi.cs:190-217 (../../SWIFT/Outgoing/SWF_OUT_MQ/InfraestructuraSwfOUTMQ/Repositorio/RepositorioTomi.cs#L190)); the schedule check also rejects an INI >= FIN window (OperacionServicio.cs:180-185).
• Time and ticks. Time is obtained through IParametrizacion rather than DateTime.Now, the shared base serializes ticks with a semaphore (no overlap), and XML documentation exists on every type and method (50 <summary> blocks).
• Test tooling is already in place (MSTest 2.2.10 + Moq), so the fix for SOM-T1 is writing tests, not introducing a framework.
