• No `TOP`/`ORDER BY`/claim: all INI rows are returned every tick in unspecified order, with no lock or marker, so two overlapping processes (restart overlap, a second host, a manual run) can read and publish the same rows; the "in use" marker is the only guard and was not verified. An unbounded read also makes the 60 s stop window unrealistic (SOM-A3).
• Join cardinality: nothing in the scripts for this solution shows that (folio, tipo) is unique in tb_srv_swf_trabajo (no DDL for the two tables was found). If a folio has more than one work row, the folio is published more than once and each second SNDNG update would overwrite an earlier PROC.
• `NOT IN ('MT-998')` silently drops rows whose NF_CVE_MENSAJE is NULL (comparison with NULL is unknown); excluded MT-998 rows stay INI forever - who consumes them is not documented here.
• No `@@ROWCOUNT` check in the two status writers: a wrong or missing folio "succeeds", so a typo cannot be detected by the caller (and PROC is described as "procesando" in the header although it is written *after* the message was sent).
• Procedures log errors to Auditoria.ErrorLog and THROW (good), but there is no reason/attempt column for ERROR rows (SOM-I4).
Fix/benefit: one atomic claim procedure (UPDATE TOP (@Max) ... OUTPUT), an explicit uniqueness constraint or a SELECT DISTINCT, IS NULL-safe filtering, @@ROWCOUNT = 1 assertions and a reason/attempt column. Coordinate with the SQL owners; deploy with SOM-I1. Suggested JIRA: SOM-S1 (P2).
SOM-D1 - Near-copy of the SWF_OUT_MQ_GCMS solution (and a third copy), already drifting (GEN-4)
Severity: Minor (P2). Category: rewrite_recommended. Checklist: duplication. Evidence (non-blank trimmed lines of this solution that also occur in the twin): ServiceHost 93 % (114/123), MQErrorHandler 86 %, RepositorioTomi 81 % (236/293), ConstantesServicio 68 %, OperacionServicio 67 %, tests 34 %. A third folder, SWIFT\Outgoing\SWF_OUT_TMP, carries yet another copy of the GCMS variant.
